        "id": 1,
        "topic": "React Native",
        "question": "What is React Native, and how does it differ from React?",
        "answer": "React Native is a framework that allows developers to build mobile applications using JavaScript and React. Unlike React, which is used for web applications, React Native renders components using native mobile UI elements instead of HTML.",
        "keyPoints": [
            "React Native enables cross-platform mobile app development.",
            "Uses native UI components instead of HTML elements.",
            "Allows JavaScript code to interact with native APIs.",
            "Shares a large part of its logic with React but uses different components."
        ],
        "codeExample": "import { Text, View } from 'react-native';\nfunction App() {\n  return <View><Text>Hello, React Native!</Text></View>;\n}",
        "resources": [
            {
                "name": "React Native Official Docs",
                "url": "https://reactnative.dev/docs/getting-started"
            }
        ],
        "tags": [
